        "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Get ready Traveler!</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In this 2D casual sandbox game, you will embark on a journey all over the world. You will buy and sell materials in the cities you visit. You will track price fluctuations in cities to maximize profit. You will get occasional negotiation opportunities. You will experience incidents, your meat can be rotten, glass can be broken and more... Your materials can be stolen. Cities will have disasters that will effect prices and amounts of some materials. The concept is simple.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But the game is chaotic. There are probabilities for price increase or decrease, price fluctuation amount, newly distributed materials, material incidents, disasters and negotiation opportunities.  The good news is: You can adjust ALL of them at the start of a new game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game has no practical ending. You will have to upgrade your storage size to fit more materials and it will cost you money. If you end up with zero or negative amount of money and lose all your materials, you will lose. If you have materials but your money decreases to -100, you will lose. If you can somehow gather &quot;<strong>NINE QUINTILLION, TWO HUNDRED TWENTY-THREE QUADRILLION, THREE HUNDRED SEVENTY-TWO TRILLION, THIRTY-SIX BILLION, EIGHT HUNDRED FIFTY-FOUR MILLION, SEVEN HUNDRED SEVENTY-FIVE THOUSAND, EIGHT HUNDRED EIGHT</strong>&quot; amount of money, you will break the game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >So, start your journey with a small backpack and try to reach that number traveler. Good luck!</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Get ready Traveler!</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In this 2D casual sandbox game, you will embark on a journey all over the world. You will buy and sell materials in the cities you visit. You will track price fluctuations in cities to maximize profit. You will get occasional negotiation opportunities. You will experience incidents, your meat can be rotten, glass can be broken and more... Your materials can be stolen. Cities will have disasters that will effect prices and amounts of some materials. The concept is simple.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But the game is chaotic. There are probabilities for price increase or decrease, price fluctuation amount, newly distributed materials, material incidents, disasters and negotiation opportunities.  The good news is: You can adjust ALL of them at the start of a new game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game has no practical ending. You will have to upgrade your storage size to fit more materials and it will cost you money. If you end up with zero or negative amount of money and lose all your materials, you will lose. If you have materials but your money decreases to -100, you will lose. If you can somehow gather &quot;<strong>NINE QUINTILLION, TWO HUNDRED TWENTY-THREE QUADRILLION, THREE HUNDRED SEVENTY-TWO TRILLION, THIRTY-SIX BILLION, EIGHT HUNDRED FIFTY-FOUR MILLION, SEVEN HUNDRED SEVENTY-FIVE THOUSAND, EIGHT HUNDRED EIGHT</strong>&quot; amount of money, you will break the game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >So, start your journey with a small backpack and try to reach that number traveler. Good luck!</p>",
